# Compiled Go binaries. None of this belongs in the repo — the Dockerfiles build
# their own binaries from source, so a checked-in artifact is always stale.

# Everything `make build` / `make build-mock` produces. Both targets write here
# precisely so a single rule covers them on every OS.
bin/

# Windows binaries wherever they land. `make build` wrote llm-proxy.exe to the
# module root before the bin/ change, and one is still sitting on disk.
*.exe

# Extensionless Linux equivalents, from a direct `go build` without -o.
/llm-proxy
/mockupstream.bin

# DO NOT add "/mockupstream" here. That is the SOURCE PACKAGE DIRECTORY for the
# mock upstream server, and a bare entry would silently exclude the entire
# package from git — the build target writes to bin/ for exactly this reason.

# Go test and coverage artifacts.
*.test
coverage.out
coverage.html
